# Corpus prose

This package is readings, not engine docs. Do not apply `.cursor/rules/copy.mdc`
or `docs/editorial-voice.md` to essay text, writer sheets, or review sheets.

Before writing or editing corpus entries, read
`packages/caelus-corpus/pipeline/voice-sheet.md`. Length bands, banned phrases,
and duplication are enforced by `src/lint.ts`; the review pass judges the rest.

## Voice

- Second person, present tense. "You" early and often.
- Theme first, then the life areas the configuration actually touches.
- Non-fatalistic, full weight. No doom, no promises, no flattery.
- No medical, financial, or legal directives.
- Plain speech. Flesch-Kincaid grade 12 or lower per entry.
- Astrology from the tradition, written fresh. No invented doctrine.
- The text must never claim a fact the selector does not guarantee.

## Do not

- Rewrite essays into the dry-engineer docs register.
- Open or close a family with the same move.
- Invent cell ids, selectors, or atom ids; copy them from the grid.
